    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Analyze the lead below and generate a professional, concise lead qualification report.\n\nLead Details:\nName: {{ $json[\"Full Name\"] }}\nEmail: {{ $json[\"Email Address\"] }}\nPhone: {{ $json[\"Phone Number\"] }}\nCompany: {{ $json[\"Company Name\"] }}\nInterested Service: {{ $json[\"Interested Service\"] }}\nBudget: {{ $json[\"Budget\"] }}\nRequirement: {{ $json[\"Describe your requirement or project briefly\"] }}\n\nLEAD QUALIFICATION RULES:\n\nHOT (75–100):\n- The prospect has a clearly defined business requirement.\n- Shows high urgency or wants implementation soon.\n- Has an approved or realistic budget, especially above ₹1 lakh.\n- Shows strong purchase intent or readiness to proceed.\n- Multiple strong buying signals should be present.\n- If the name/company/email looks like a test or placeholder, mention verification in the analysis and recommended action. Do not automatically downgrade an otherwise strong lead solely because of a test-like name.\n\nWARM (40–74):\n- Shows genuine interest and has a reasonably clear requirement.\n- May have a budget but needs clarification, discovery, verification, or planning.\n- Has moderate urgency or is evaluating solutions.\n- Purchase intent is not yet fully confirmed.\n- The prospect is considering a solution but has not shown strong immediate buying intent.\n\nCOLD (0–39):\n- Requirement is vague or exploratory.\n- No meaningful urgency or purchase intent.\n- Budget is absent, very low, or unrealistic.\n- The prospect is only researching or showing minimal interest.\n- The prospect explicitly says they are only exploring, have no budget, have no urgency, and are not planning to purchase currently.\n\nSTRICT COLD CLASSIFICATION:\nIf the lead states:\n- No current budget\n- No urgency\n- Only exploring or researching\n- No immediate purchasing plans\n\nThen classify the lead as COLD and assign a score between 0 and 39.\n\nDo not classify such a lead as Warm merely because they submitted the form or expressed general interest.\n\nSCORING GUIDELINES:\n- Budget: 0–25 points\n- Urgency: 0–25 points\n- Requirement clarity: 0–20 points\n- Purchase intent/readiness: 0–20 points\n- Business credibility/contact verification: 0–10 points\n\nThe final qualification MUST follow the score:\n75–100 = Hot\n40–74 = Warm\n0–39 = Cold\n\nReturn exactly this structure:\n\nLEAD QUALIFICATION: [Hot/Warm/Cold]\nLEAD SCORE: [Score]/100\n\nREQUIREMENT ANALYSIS:\n[Brief analysis in 2-3 sentences explaining the requirement, urgency, budget, buying intent, and any verification concerns.]\n\nRECOMMENDED NEXT ACTION:\n[One clear action appropriate to the qualification. Hot = prioritize immediate contact/discovery call. Warm = personalized follow-up/discovery. Cold = nurturing or low-priority follow-up.]\n\nEMAIL SUBJECT:\n[Professional personalized subject]\n\nEMAIL BODY:\n[Write one personalized email. Include greeting, acknowledge the requirement, explain how we can help, and suggest a short discovery call. Match the tone to the lead qualification. End with a professional signature: The AI Solutions Team.]\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Generate only ONE email.\n- Do not repeat the report.\n- Do not generate multiple email versions.\n- Be realistic and evidence-based when scoring.\n- Do not classify every lead as Warm by default.\n- High budget + strong urgency + clear implementation requirement + approved budget should generally qualify as Hot.\n- Treat test/demo names cautiously and mention verification if necessary.\n- Keep the response professional and concise.\n- Use exactly the words Hot, Warm, or Cold in the qualification label.\n- Do not include markdown formatting symbols.\n- Do not invent information that is not provided.",
        "options": {}
      },
